{"resourceIdentifier":"2998","resourceName":"Brascarbon Methane Recovery Project BCA-BRA-16","description":"The purpose of this project is to mitigate and recover animal effluent related Greenhouse Gas (GHG) by improving the Animal Waste Management System practices in the confined animal feed operations in the cities located at the Mato Grosso do Sul state, central Brazil, developed by BRASCARBON. In Brazil the agricultural operations related to the confined animals procedures are very wide and grow progressively and intensive to attend the worldwide food demand. There are three types of Confined Animal Operation for this project: finishing, breeding and nursery. \r\nThe scenario existing prior to the implementation of the project activity is the same as the baseline scenario, as follows: the confined animal wastewater, which consists of fresh water mixed with manure and urine that accumulates in pits under or beside the barns, is transported to one open lagoon for evaporation, fed by gravity pipeline systems. The organic material degraded in the primary treatment lagoon is digested, thereby producing significant amounts of methane. These systems emit methane (CH4) resulting from anaerobic decomposition process. The swine livestock operations create profound environmental consequences, such as greenhouse gas emissions, odour and water/land contamination that result of storing animal waste, where this operation is not sustainable due to its sever environmental pollution.\r\nThe Project Activity consists in the construction of a new covered in-ground anaerobic reactor (digester) that will utilize the organic material currently treated in the wastewater opened lagoon, of the confined animal operations to produce biogas. All manure will be sent daily directly to digester not exceeding 24 hours in the barns.","location":{"latitude":-19.395000,"longitude":-54.565833},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2022-07-01","endExclusive":"2022-08-01","endInclusive":"2022-07-31"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"2998"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Mato Grosso do Sul"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Brascarbon Consultoria Projetos e Representacao S/A"},{"type":"string","value":"São Paulo, Brazil"},{"type":"string","value":"+5511989017810"},{"type":"string","value":"mario.silva@brascarbon.com.br"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"2998"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"55356"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Waste handling and disposal"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"AMS-III.D."}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Colombian Institute for Technical Standards and Certification (ICONTEC)"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_REGISTRATION_DATE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"23/03/2023"}]},{"code":"CREDIT_PERIOD_INFO","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1st, 02/01/2021 - 01/01/2028"}]}]}],"documentGroups":[{"code":"VCS_PIPELINE_DOCUMENTS","description":"VCS Pipeline Documents","documents":[{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=63397&IDKEY=qlksjoiuwqowrnoiuomnckjashoufifmln902309ksdflku098k87424463","documentType":"Listing Representation","documentName":"VCS-Listing-Representation-Single-Representor-v4.1_BC.pdf","uploadDate":"2022-03-15T18:03:38.747Z"}]},{"code":"VCS_REGISTRATION_DOCUMENTS","description":"VCS Registration Documents","documents":[{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=86879&IDKEY=0lksjoiuwqowrnoiuomnckjashoufifmln902309ksdflku098k119806141","documentType":"Project Description","documentName":"Brascarbon Methane Recovery 